{"event_type":"review","id":"ac80a06fbfc3c98dd122ec9c0dd54f9a69b4d47011845407f17926f86142bf3e","occurred_at":"2026-11-16T00:09:21Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c2a60803c144fc5677a89272779ed230c18cca3172d81df35f91a119e2f2a2c5","sha256":"c2a60803c144fc5677a89272779ed230c18cca3172d81df35f91a119e2f2a2c5"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e5e27e407827f234e05011b8923d88460d5ab67a303b9acee563e00bb8dd070b","sha256":"e5e27e407827f234e05011b8923d88460d5ab67a303b9acee563e00bb8dd070b"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b82277a36c21b85f7c781e86822897e68941d1b99a31650fdc03ee507338364b","sha256":"b82277a36c21b85f7c781e86822897e68941d1b99a31650fdc03ee507338364b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a31609b35e0e7ad520449a557fb8579a711a240a67965b9462b665079991911b","sha256":"a31609b35e0e7ad520449a557fb8579a711a240a67965b9462b665079991911b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6911719dd755cfa5803cc9969a4d27cf819c8c0a15f22786ca49df9a44648f10","sha256":"6911719dd755cfa5803cc9969a4d27cf819c8c0a15f22786ca49df9a44648f10"}],"attempt_id":"34592b66ff3a362f04c7c95cbd18995fb789f653b26da5834c237ae1dacd92f3:0:1","base":"802a69d0f7d57c838f839996dacc375da3a762f3","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"c7ff8ffec7b5dcf0cd3d92aee950e34abc60fdcd","body":"**Follow-up: preserve the needs-human exit code.**\n\nIf `options.live` returns `status: 'needs-human'`, Line 152 returns exit code 1 instead of 3. Map this status to 3 while preserving the artifact.\n\nAs per coding guidelines, “Exit codes: 0 clean, 1 thrown error, 2 arg error, 3 needs-human.” Based on learnings, Minor findings are deferred to follow-up issues.","id":"7344c15455e1004f1efbcbe222d1fc3186a1cd8da16d9345655362888cbcbbfc","intervals":[[152,152]],"path":"src/queue-runner/runner.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Follow-up: preserve the needs-human exit code."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"c7ff8ffec7b5dcf0cd3d92aee950e34abc60fdcd","body":"**Define `PlannerUsageError` in `runner.ts` and map it to the usage artifact.**\n\n`src/queue-runner/tick.ts:58` imports `PlannerUsageError` from `./runner.js`. `tick.ts:389` throws it when `crq tick --dry-run` receives unexpected arguments. `runner.ts` does not declare or export this class, so the import has no binding in the repository. The planner `catch` at `runner.ts:198-204` then returns `exitCode: 1` for every planner error. Argument errors should instead return the usage artifact with exit code 2, as doctrine I1 requires.\n\nDeclare and export the class in `runner.ts`. Then map it in the `catch` to the existing `usage` helper. Because `tick.ts` already imports from `runner.ts`, this adds no new import edge.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n export const LIVE_OPERATOR_COMMANDS = ['repair-prepare'] as const;\n+\n+export class PlannerUsageError extends Error {}\n```\n\n```diff\n   } catch (error) {\n+    if (error instanceof PlannerUsageError) return usage(error.message);\n     return {\n       artifact: { status: 'failed', error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error) },\n       exitCode: 1,\n```\n\n</details>","id":"96c81e4376639738a4c19b9d3e115c9fda5d15ac1e6ec62f13be8f29014c0297","intervals":[[201,201]],"path":"src/queue-runner/runner.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Define `PlannerUsageError` in `runner.ts` and map it to the usage artifact."}],"head":"c8d565fe576387089e4e531eb44c83072197da16","head_tree":"7e3bc6040d8da1acb2564424b853efe795537180","input_scope":[{"blob":"ed7fbeb1ad66dbafd1c4ced0492951cb2a54e792","intervals":[[1,29]],"path":"src/queue-runner/crq.ts"},{"blob":"c7ff8ffec7b5dcf0cd3d92aee950e34abc60fdcd","